> bridi B is equivalent to C(B): i.e. the tense is a predicate and the

> bridi is its argument.



This interpretation seems right to me for lojban, IMO following the CLL

prescription (BTW, this is the explicit solution AFAIK used in gua!spi,

which may indicate that the tense cmavo were indeed seen as true

predicate in early Loglan or lojban).

